        "retrieval": 26.0,
        "fast_filter": 0.08,
        "validation": 2495.7,
        "generation": 10921.94,
        "total": 23353.61
      },
      "answer": "Sliding Window Backpressure is a flow-control mechanism used by the Zephyr transport protocol. It works as follows:\n\n- The receiver sends an acknowledgment header back to the sender indicating how many ring-buffer slots remain unoccupied.\n  \n- This allows the sender to halt its data transmissions before reaching the MTU size limit (default 1420 bytes).\n\n- By doing so, it prevents buffer overflow on both ends of the connection, ensuring efficient and controlled data transfer."
    },
