        "fast_filter": 1.48,
        "validation": 2953.24,
        "generation": 15718.5,
        "total": 29120.21
      },
      "answer": "During Stage Two span verification, technicians connect the manifold to a certified 1013.25 hectopascal calibration standard. They record the residual offset reported on diagnostic register 0x1A. \n\nIf the absolute offset exceeds 1.2 hectopascals, they need to replace the silicone intake gasket before retrying the span verification process. This ensures accurate data collection.\n\nAfter successfully completing the span calibration, the firmware writes the two calibration coefficients to protected EEPROM bank B and sets the status flag CAL_VERIFIED to 1.\n\nThese calibrated coefficients will then be used for subsequent operations including alert thresholds calculations and telemetry transmissions."
    },
